{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook, the social media giant that has taken over the world. directed by david fincher, the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, which chronicles the rise of mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook.\n\nthe movie starts with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, who is dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright (played by rachel taylor). in a fit of anger and hurt, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two harvard students and vote on which one is more attractive. the website becomes an instant hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the harvard administration.\n\nlater, mark is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the harvard rowing team and are looking to create a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees to help them, but eventually decides to create his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\". with the help of his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), mark launches the site, which quickly becomes a huge success.\n\nas the site grows in popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship begins to fray, and they find themselves at odds over the direction of the company. meanwhile, the winklevoss twins claim that mark stole their idea and sue him for damages.\n\nthe movie is a fascinating look at the rise of facebook and the personalities that were involved in its creation. jesse eisenberg gives a great performance as mark zuckerberg, capturing his awkwardness and intensity. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo saverin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and naivety to the role.\n\nthe supporting cast is also impressive, with armie hammer standing out as the winklevoss twins. hammer's performance is nuanced and subtle, capturing the twins' arrogance and entitlement.\n\none of the strengths of the movie is its writing, which is sharp and insightful. the dialogue is witty and engaging, and the script does a great job of capturing the complexities of the characters and their relationships.\n\nthe movie's themes are also worth noting. it's a film about ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success. mark zuckerberg is a complex character, driven by a desire to succeed, but also struggling with his own identity and sense of purpose.\n\noverall, the social network is a great movie that is both entertaining and thought-provoking. it's a fascinating look at the rise of facebook and the people who were involved in its creation. if you're interested in technology, business, or just great storytelling, this is a movie worth checking out.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.8832452893257141}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0004891153075732291}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.006715467199683189}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -2.644798755645752}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0034202192910015583}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.7945298552513123}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.31326478719711304}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.0006764031131751835}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.541770613286644e-05}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.4740769863128662}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.006917811930179596}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.10317980498075485}, {"token": " media", "logprob": -0.0005529781919904053}, {"token": " giant", "logprob": -0.20141518115997314}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00013064485392533243}, 